  "claim": "borg_flow_light(), borg_flow_vault() and borg_excavate_vault() loop over the visible panel, w_y .. w_y + SCREEN_HGT and w_x .. w_x + SCREEN_WID, and index borg_grids[y][x], which has AUTO_MAX_Y (66) rows of AUTO_MAX_X (198) grids. SCREEN_HGT and SCREEN_WID follow the terminal size; when the panel is larger than the level, modify_panel() clamps the origin to 0 and the loops run past the map. On a 70-row terminal the original reads borg_grids[66] and [67] (AddressSanitizer: global-buffer-overflow READ of size 8) and the normal build crashes; on a 230-column terminal it reads 18 grids past each row (heap-buffer-overflow READ) silently. Bounding both loops by AUTO_MAX_Y / AUTO_MAX_X removes every report; standard-terminal and exact-fit controls are byte-identical.",
